---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="Vezne Privacy Policy — how Vezne collects, uses, and protects your data (KVKK & GDPR)."
	lastUpdated="24 July 2026"
>
	<section>
		<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
		<p>
			This Privacy Policy explains how Vezne ("we," "us") collects,
			uses, and protects your personal data when you use the Service.
			For the purposes of applicable data protection law — including
			Turkey's Law on the Protection of Personal Data No. 6698 ("KVKK")
			and, where relevant, the EU General Data Protection Regulation
			("GDPR") — Vezne acts as the data controller. You can reach us at
			<strong>privacy@vezne.app</strong> for any privacy question or
			to exercise the rights described below.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Account data:</strong> your email address and password
				(stored as a salted hash — we never store or see your plain-text
				password).
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Financial data you provide:</strong> the transactions,
				categories, tags, and categorization rules you create, and the
				content of bank statement files you choose to import
				(date, amount, description, and similar fields).
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Usage data:</strong> basic account activity such as when
				you last used the Service, used internally to operate and
				secure your account.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			We don't ask for your name, phone number, address, or date of
			birth, and we don't request your bank login credentials, card
			numbers, or IBAN — imports are files you upload yourself, not a
			live connection to your bank.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>3. Why we process your data</h2>
		<p>
			We process account and financial data because it's necessary to
			provide the Service you've asked for — creating your account,
			storing and displaying your transactions, and running the
			features you use (KVKK Art. 5, GDPR Art. 6(1)(b) — performance of
			a contract). Where we ask for a separate, specific opt-in — for
			example, enabling AI-assisted PDF parsing — we rely on your
			consent (KVKK Art. 5, GDPR Art. 6(1)(a)), which you can withdraw
			at any time in Settings.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>4. Who else sees your data</h2>
		<p>
			We don't sell your data or share it for advertising. A small
			number of third-party services help us run Vezne, and each only
			receives what it needs to do its job:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Sign-in provider:</strong> if you choose to sign in with
				Google instead of a password, that provider handles the
				authentication step. We only receive your verified email
				address back.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Bot-detection / abuse-prevention service:</strong> a
				challenge shown on the sign-up form to keep the Service free of
				automated abuse. It processes standard browser/network signals,
				not your financial data.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Error-tracking service:</strong> used so we can find and
				fix bugs. It's configured to not collect personal information by
				default, and requests to authentication endpoints are excluded
				from what it sees entirely.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>AI parsing service (optional, off by default):</strong>
				if you turn on AI-assisted PDF import in Settings, the content
				of the PDF bank statement you upload is sent to this service to
				help extract transaction rows. This only happens for PDF files,
				and only if you've explicitly enabled it — it's off for every
				account by default, and CSV/Excel imports never use it.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Because some of these providers may process data outside Turkey,
			your data may be transferred internationally as a result of using
			these features, subject to those providers' own safeguards. Exact
			provider names are available on request — contact us using the
			details in Section 1.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>5. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
		<p>
			Vezne doesn't use cookies for tracking or advertising, and we
			don't run any analytics. Your sign-in session is kept in your
			browser's local storage, which is strictly necessary for the
			Service to work (keeping you signed in) and doesn't require a
			separate cookie-consent banner. The third-party services listed
			above may set their own strictly-necessary technical identifiers
			when their features are active (e.g. the bot-detection widget).
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>6. How long we keep your data</h2>
		<p>
			We keep your account and financial data for as long as your
			account is active. If you delete your account from Settings, it's
			deactivated immediately and kept for 30 days in case you want to
			restore it by signing back in. After 30 days, your categories,
			tags, transactions, and rules are permanently deleted, and your
			account record is anonymized.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>7. Your rights</h2>
		<p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Ask us what personal data we hold about you, and get a copy.</li>
			<li>Ask us to correct inaccurate data.</li>
			<li>
				Ask us to delete your data — you can already do this yourself
				from Settings → Delete account.
			</li>
			<li>Object to or restrict certain processing.</li>
			<li>
				Withdraw consent you previously gave (e.g. for AI-assisted PDF
				import), without affecting processing that happened before you
				withdrew it.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			These correspond to the rights set out in KVKK Art. 11 and, for
			users in the European Economic Area, GDPR Art. 15-22. To exercise
			any of them, contact us using the details in Section 1. If you're
			in Turkey, you can also apply to the Personal Data Protection
			Board (Kişisel Verileri Koruma Kurulu); if you're in the EEA, you
			can lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>8. Security</h2>
		<p>
			We use industry-standard measures to protect your data, including
			encrypted connections (TLS) between your browser and our servers,
			salted password hashing, and access controls that keep every
			account's data isolated from every other account's.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>9. Children</h2>
		<p>
			Vezne is not directed to, and we don't knowingly collect data
			from, children. If you believe a child has created an account,
			contact us and we'll take appropriate action.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
		<p>
			We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material
			changes will be reflected in the "Last updated" date above and,
			where appropriate, announced through the Service.
		</p>
	</section>
</LegalLayout>
